s.t:
Learn from our experienced professionals and work on real-world projects.
Develop skills in performance optimization, our core area of expertise, while building a diverse skillset.
Engage in a variety of missions, adapting to different client needs and technological challenges.
Work with cutting-edge technologies and contribute to Crossjoin's mission of delivering top-tier solutions.
Benefit from our commitment to continuous learning with mentoring training, and certifications in the latest technologies. You’ll become a specialist in a high-demand field, building a career with immense growth potential.
Required Skills & Competencies
Bachelor’s or Master’s in Computer Science or similar field;
No professional experience needed;
Understand different concepts around programming languages like Java, C, C++, Python, and SQL;
Understand different variations around databases SQL and NoSQL, like MySQL, PostgreSQL, Cassandra, MongoDB;
Excellent communication, resilient and goal-oriented;
Driven by technology and challenges;
Be able to write and speak in English;
Be able to travel.

Translate user stories and business requirements into working Mendix applications (domain models, flows, pages, security roles);
Build integrations with internal and external systems via APIs and database connectors, and implement single sign-on (SAML/OIDC);
Develop reusable modules, widgets and components in line with GSC standards, and contribute to a shared component library;
Apply secure-by-design practices, role-based access control and data protection requirements;
Build accessible interfaces that meet WCAG 2.1 AA;
Write unit and automated tests, take part in code reviews, and use the Mendix Quality Add-ons or equivalent to keep technical debt under control;
Support deployment, release management and third-level maintenance of applications in production;
Produce and maintain technical documentation.

University degree in IT and 5 years of IT development experience, including at least 3 years hands-on with Mendix;
Proven delivery of at least two Mendix applications into production, including integration with enterprise systems;
Experience with Mendix 10 or later, on-premises or private cloud deployment;
Working knowledge of Java and JavaScript for custom actions and widgets;
Experience working in Scrum or similar agile frameworks;
Mendix Advanced Developer certification would be required & Mendix Expert certification will be considered as an asset;
Experience with Mendix AI capabilities (e.g. GenAI connectors, Maia) will be considered as an asset;
Knowledge of French will be considered as an asset;
Excellent command of the English language.
